<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107027" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπειδόμην</span></b> , aor.
		
			Med.
		 (inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπιδέσθαι,</span>
		part.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπιδόμενος,</span> in codd. freq. written
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείδεσθαι, -ειδόμενος,</span> as if
		from a pres.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείδομαι,</span> which is found in late Gr.,
			v. infr. <i><span class="en">
			111
		</span></i>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>view from
				below, behold,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				694
			</span></i>; of a prophetic vision, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν τύχην θ᾽
				ὑπειδόμην τὴν σήν, ἃ πείσῃ τ᾽</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
				60.37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>mistrust, suspect,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1023
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.66.6
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>perceive, detect,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				429
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>seem,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃ ὑπείδεταί πως εἰπεῖν</span> which
			he <i>appears</i> to mean, ib.<i><span class="en">
				345
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
